<title>UK: Queensborough buys Granada park.</title>
<headline>Queensborough buys Granada park.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Caravan parks to hotels group Queensborough Holdings Plc has bought a leisure park from the Granada Group Plc, industry sources said on Monday.</p>
<p>The source said Granada has sold the American Theme Park in Derby.</p>
<p>While Granada officials were not immediately available for comment, an industry source close to the negotiations told Reuters, &quot;the deal has been done&quot;.</p>
<p>The price of sale could not be confirmed but Monday's London Evening Standard said it was valued at three million stg.</p>
<p>The newspaper said Granada was also due to sell its Camelot attraction near Chorley in Lancashire. A buyer has not been identified in that deal.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
